  "scope": "Exact source and quadrature identities are checked in the actual finite six-mode simplex model, retaining its noncommuting clock and source. Complete coupled coordinate transport and norm-preserving transverse pullback concern the stated commuting differential expression. Lean proves the Gaussian weighted-energy divergence, independently of tail samples, and exact directional derivative-energy scaling. The resulting obstruction excludes this Gaussian product ansatz with nonzero transverse derivative energy; it is not a no-go theorem for all domains. An explicit additional negative-tail damping factor restores this weighted derivative energy, as proved in Lean by Gaussian domination and change of variables. Its exponential-longitudinal domain membership is not yet proved. Infinite operator identification, a full common finite-energy domain, capacity and regulator limits, physical identification and the TOE remain open."
